<!DOCTYPE html>
<html><head><link type="text/css" rel="stylesheet" href="/tracker/style.css"> </link><script type="text/javascript" src="/tracker/script.js"> </script><title>CVE-2026-115560</title></head><body><header><h1>CVE-2026-115560</h1></header><table><tr><td><b>Name</b></td><td>CVE-2026-115560</td></tr><tr><td><b>Description</b></td><td>Session serializer mismatch can lead to remote code execution.  Session upload progress, when enabled, can store attacker-controlled data in a session key using the php_binary or php_serialize session serializer. If the same session is later read with the php serializer, because session.serialize_handler is changed at runtime or differs between applications sharing a session store, bytes inside the key can be passed to the unserializer. A remote attacker able to submit a multipart upload can inject objects, which may lead to code execution when the reading application contains a suitable gadget chain, or to session corruption or denial of service.  This issue affects PHP versions before 8.2.36, 8.3.* before 8.3.37, 8.4.* before 8.4.28 and 8.5.* before 8.5.13.</td></tr><tr><td><b>Source</b></td><td><a href="https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-115560">CVE</a> (at <a href="https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-115560">NVD</a>; <a href="https://www.kb.cert.org/vuls/byid?searchview=&amp;query=CVE-2026-115560">CERT</a>, <a href="https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/vulnerability/CVE-2026-115560">ENISA</a>, <a href="https://lwn.net/Search/DoSearch?words=CVE-2026-115560">LWN</a>, <a href="https://marc.info/?l=oss-security&amp;s=CVE-2026-115560">oss-sec</a>, <a href="https://marc.info/?l=full-disclosure&amp;s=CVE-2026-115560">fulldisc</a>, <a href="https://deb.freexian.com/extended-lts/tracker/CVE-2026-115560">Debian ELTS</a>, <a href="https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2026-115560">Red Hat</a>, <a href="https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-115560">Ubuntu</a>, <a href="https://bugs.gentoo.org/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2026-115560">Gentoo</a>, SUSE <a href="https://bugzilla.suse.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2026-115560">bugzilla</a>/<a href="https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-115560/">CVE</a>, GitHub <a href="https://github.com/advisories?query=CVE-2026-115560">advisories</a>/<a href="https://github.com/search?type=Code&amp;q=%22CVE-2026-115560%22">code</a>/<a href="https://github.com/search?type=Issues&amp;q=%22CVE-2026-115560%22">issues</a>, <a href="https://duckduckgo.com/html?q=%22CVE-2026-115560%22">web search</a>, <a href="https://oss-security.openwall.org/wiki/vendors">more</a>)</td></tr><tr><td><b>References</b></td><td><a href="/tracker/DLA-4916-1">DLA-4916-1</a>, <a href="/tracker/DSA-6641-1">DSA-6641-1</a></td></tr></table><h2>Vulnerable and fixed packages</h2><p>The table below lists information on source packages.</p><table><tr><th>Source Package</th><th>Release</th><th>Version</th><th>Status</th></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.2">php8.2</a> (<a href="https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/php8.2">PTS</a>)</td><td>bookworm</td><td><span class="red">8.2.32-1~deb12u1</span></td><td><span class="red">vulnerable</span></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>bookworm (security)</td><td>8.2.36-1~deb12u1</td><td>fixed</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.4">php8.4</a> (<a href="https://tracker.debian.org/pkg/php8.4">PTS</a>)</td><td>trixie</td><td><span class="red">8.4.27-1~deb13u1</span></td><td><span class="red">vulnerable</span></td></tr><tr><td></td><td>trixie (security)</td><td>8.4.28-1~deb13u1</td><td>fixed</td></tr><tr><td></td><td>forky, sid</td><td>8.4.28-3</td><td>fixed</td></tr></table><p>The information below is based on the following data on fixed versions.</p><table><tr><th>Package</th><th>Type</th><th>Release</th><th>Fixed Version</th><th>Urgency</th><th>Origin</th><th>Debian Bugs</th></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.2">php8.2</a></td><td>source</td><td>bookworm</td><td>8.2.36-1~deb12u1</td><td></td><td><a href="/tracker/DLA-4916-1">DLA-4916-1</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.2">php8.2</a></td><td>source</td><td>(unstable)</td><td><span class="red">(unfixed)</span></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.4">php8.4</a></td><td>source</td><td>trixie</td><td>8.4.28-1~deb13u1</td><td></td><td><a href="/tracker/DSA-6641-1">DSA-6641-1</a></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><a href="/tracker/source-package/php8.4">php8.4</a></td><td>source</td><td>(unstable)</td><td>8.4.28-2</td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table><h2>Notes</h2><pre><a href="https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx">https://github.com/php/php-src/security/advisories/GHSA-658j-r8rw-q6mx</a><br/></pre><hr/><form method="get" id="searchform" action="/tracker/">Search for package or bug name: <input type="text" name="query" onkeyup="onSearch(this.value)" onmousemove="onSearch(this.value)"/><input type="submit" value="Go"/> <a href="/tracker/data/report">Reporting problems</a></form><footer><p><a href="/tracker/">Home</a> - <a href="https://www.debian.org/security/">Debian Security</a> - <a href="https://salsa.debian.org/security-tracker-team/security-tracker/blob/master/bin/tracker_service.py">Source</a> <a href="https://salsa.debian.org/security-tracker-team/security-tracker">(Git)</a></p></footer></body></html>